message:
{{#is_alert}}{{value}}% of payment requests are failing at the transport level. These are broken authorisation attempts, not refused cards — the guest gets an error page rather than "your card was declined".{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}Payment error rate is {{value}}%, past the {{warn_threshold}}% warning line.{{/is_warning}}

**Errors are not declines, and the difference decides who owns this.** A decline is a correct business outcome the provider chose and is recorded as such; an error means the conversation with the provider broke and we do not know what happened. 05-FUNCTIONALITY.md § 11 keeps them on separate flags (`payment_error_rate` versus `payment_decline_rate`) precisely so this distinction can be demonstrated. *Voyager — Checkout Deep Dive* → *Authorised vs declined vs errored per minute* shows all three lines side by side; read it before escalating.

**Likely cause.** The provider returning 5xx, timing out, or the call failing before it is made. Check *Provider latency p95 by operation* on the same dashboard: errors with high latency means the provider is overloaded, errors with normal latency means it is refusing fast.

**Watch for the second-order effect.** Failed authorisations are retried, and retries hit the idempotency layer. Rising `voyager.payment.idempotency_replays` alongside this alert is the safety net doing its job — it is what stops a retry becoming a double charge. If replays are *not* rising while errors are, that is worth investigating on its own.

**Chaos flag that reverses it.** `payment_error_rate` makes `mock-payments` return 500 — explicitly an error, not a decline. Scenario **S2** sets it to 0.30 along with `payment_latency_ms=3000`, `payment_decline_rate=0.25`, `payment_decline_mix=insufficient_funds` and `payment_webhook_delay_ms=15000`. Clear just this with `scripts/chaos.sh set payment_error_rate 0`, or unwind the brownout with `scripts/chaos.sh revert S2`.

This monitor is one half of the composite **[Voyager] Checkout degraded**, which only fires when payment errors and falling booking throughput happen together.
{{#is_recovery}}Payment error rate is back under 5%. Reconcile anything left in `PENDING_PAYMENT` before closing.{{/is_recovery}}
